    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability. The ASAN report confirms the heap-buffer-overflow at `fasthuf_read_bits` line 1186, called from `fasthuf_initialize` line 1284 (the LONG_ZEROCODE_RUN branch), called from `internal_huf_decompress` line 1799.\n\nThe crash reads 1 byte past a 45-byte heap allocation (the 37-byte Huffman data + 4 bytes PIZ header + 4 bytes hufbytes field = 45 bytes of chunk data read into the buffer).\n\nThe PoC is a 338-byte OpenEXR file with PIZ compression containing a crafted Huffman table where:\n- 15 zero bytes consume symbols 0-19 as zero-length codes\n- Byte 15 (0x03) provides a zero code length for symbol 20, with bottom 2 bits seeding value 63\n- Byte 16 (0xFF) completes the 6-bit read as 63 (LONG_ZEROCODE_RUN) at symbol 21\n- The subsequent 8-bit read for the run length advances `currByte` past the buffer end",
